@participant1 It's annoying yes but we shouldn't lash out at the developers. They likely have better things to do even if this issue is the most pressing one to us...

bump

Also tested with [v32](https://gist.github.com/reporter/e291915f2dd447b643317e0b63180988) and [v33-beta](https://gist.github.com/reporter/6303113f139e71a0079fa12af0aab054)

It seems this issue also happens when vibrancy is off and you use backdrop filter on the body element.

I suggest to ditch the vibrancy property and instead use a fake background by using a gradient background image then apply a backdrop filter on it.

```css
  body {
    @apply bg-[#191920];
    background-image: url(/public/gradient-grainy-gradient-background.jpg);
    background-blend-mode: multiply;
    background-size: cover;
  }

  #root {
    @apply backdrop-blur;
  }

```

@participant6 I'm well aware of that fact, that's why [this](https://<redacted-host>/u/1/issues/380416865) issue exists
Both of your solutions aren't solutions in my book as I actually want a transparent background (:
I only keep this issue open to not need to open a new one once the chromium issue is resolved and it still doesn't work with electron for a different reason.
